1. As a child, she was not allowed to drink anything with her meals, including water, due to a family rule from her British side. (Verbatim: "as a kid i straight up wasn't allowed to have a drink whenever i had meals... it was from no not even water like just no drink why i don't know it was nana elia's rule because it came from my um dad's side so from my british side")

2. She has a family nickname, "Nana Elia," which refers to a relative on her father’s British side who enforced strict mealtime rules. (Verbatim: "it was nana elia's rule because it came from my um dad's side so from my british side")

3. She struggled with finishing meals as a child and is a slow eater. (Verbatim: "yeah i am a really slow eater i straight up really struggled to finish... meals")

4. Her father, referred to as "Papa Elia," has misophonia and could not eat at the dinner table due to being disturbed by eating sounds. (Verbatim: "papa elia doesn't like me eating near because he has misophonia... he actually never ate at the dinner table like yeah would sit elsewhere")

5. Because of her father’s misophonia, she learned to chew very slowly to minimize noise during meals. (Verbatim: "that's also why i had to learn how to chew really really slowly though because if you chew slowly you make um you make less noise")

6. She finds it difficult to eat meals without a drink and has always wanted a drink with food, which felt like a struggle growing up. (Verbatim: "i struggle to have meals if there's no drink to go with it like i struggle but the thing is as a kid i straight up wasn't allowed to have a drink")

7. The rule of no drinks during meals applied not only to her but also to her siblings and extended family members during their upbringing. (Verbatim: "it wasn't just me like it was apparently the same rules that like my uncles and aunties had growing up and the same rules that my brothers had")

8. She has a preference for peppercorn sauce on steak. (Verbatim: "i do like peppercorn sauce sauce sauce yeah yeah yeah i do like peppercorn sauce")

9. She once saw someone walking through her parents’ garden as a shortcut, which frightened her and felt invasive. (Verbatim: "i remember i was looking up my window once and i saw someone going through the garden and it freaked me the heck out because i was like someone was like using my parents garden is like a shortcut")

10. She associates certain visual styles with bad mobile game ads, indicating a familiarity with or strong opinion about mobile game design tropes. (Verbatim: "this feels like one of those like really bad mobile game adverts you know like just the font and how it looks and everything just gives me that vibe") [end of text]



