6. She has a habit of forgetting to eat, especially when focused on work, and used to skip dinner in favor of sleeping during her student days. (Verbatim: "when I was a student, I remember thinking, 'Oh, what should I have for dinner?' 'Oh, nothing. I'll sleep.' So I think I just trained myself to sleep instead of eat.")

7. She enjoys paninis and mentions they are commonly available at most coffee shops in England, particularly from a smaller, unnamed chain. (Verbatim: "Now you can get paninis from like every coffee shop in England, I would say. Like most, most coffee shops in England have paninis.")

8. She associates her time in America with learning about "freedom," which she now frequently references. (Verbatim: "This is what I learned from my time in America by the way if y'all were wondering like where I learned freedom from. Yeah. Went to America, learned freedom, came back.")

9. She jokes about being "stinky" and refers to everyone, including herself and her audience, as stinky in a self-deprecating manner. (Verbatim: "You're both stinky. You're all stinky. We're all stinky.")

10. She owns cat ears merchandise and has purchased many of them on Discord, which triggered security checks. (Verbatim: "Discord didn't expect someone to have so many kittens. I know, right?") [end of text]



